E-2002 made both halves normalize identically;

The point is legibility of 'endless sql' output, which is a supported surface.

The trap to design around: today one function returns the canonical form AND that value is passed to os.Stat, filepath.Join and git.

Two root causes, same shape: what the agent is told at a decision point decides what it does next.

(1) The spawn handoff's 'could it reasonably be done now, inside the work already underway?' reads as a topical purity test, so a cheap unrelated fix falls through to 'otherwise file it';

(2) Every status-affecting task update prints a status change plus a --keep-status advisory, both addressed to the agent, which relays them and spends user attention;

Both surfaced live on E-2114.
